# GitHub reads this file to render the "Cite this repository" button.
# Spec: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this collection or its taxonomy is useful in your work, you can cite it
  as below. Please cite the individual papers as well — this record covers the
  classification work, not the research it organizes.
title: "Awesome Agentic Systems: a classified collection of papers on agentic AI systems"
abstract: >-
  A curated, machine-validated collection of papers on LLM-based agentic
  systems. Each paper is filed under exactly one area describing its
  contribution, and cut across by a flat topic vocabulary and five facets
  (about, scale, type, infra, domain). The taxonomy is derived from
  published surveys and is validated at build time, so no record can carry a
  term outside the declared vocabulary.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: dos Reis
    given-names: Julio Cesar
repository-code: https://github.com/juliodosreis/awesome-agenticsystems
url: https://juliodosreis.com/awesome-agenticsystems
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - agentic-ai
  - multi-agent-systems
  - taxonomy
  - literature-review
